WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.060
I am Carla Fou Wayne.

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:05.730
Pleasure to meet you, my lord.

00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:08.360
<i>Carla Wayne?</i>

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:14.240
My lord, please save the Wayne family.

00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:17.020
Please save us.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:28.420
<b>Trapped in</b>

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:30.760
<b>a Dating Sim</b>

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:35.390
<b>Trapped in
a Dating Sim</b>

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:56.190
Master, are you really 
going to help that girl?

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:58.780
We Both Hate Hot Guys

00:01:56.190 --> 00:01:59.130
We have several days off 
after the school festival.

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:00.760
I'll go help her then.

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:03.760
But I see no compelling 
reason for you to help her.

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:09.150
I don't, either, but she officially 
requested my assistance.

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:15.530
Since Livia acted as an intermediary, 
if I refused to help her, Livia will lose face.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:19.230
Both Livia and I have already gotten 
caught up in whatever's going on.

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:27.820
Don't things seem awkward between those two?

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:30.540
Maybe it's because of 
what happened yesterday.

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:33.870
You think you can stand 
on equal footing with us?

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:37.420
Just because you're 
Angelica's cute little pet?

00:02:38.310 --> 00:02:39.800
Her pet?

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:45.300
Maybe I'll give them a break.

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:47.810
I think that's a good idea. 
The shop's not busy, anyway.

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:51.060
We're deep in the red, though.

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:54.440
Don't worry about it. 
We'll make a killing on the last day.

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:55.570
Doing what?

00:02:55.570 --> 00:02:57.450
You don't mean...

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:01.700
It's finally time.

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:03.660
Well, it <i>is</i> the highlight 
of the school festival.

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:05.700
Who's going to win this year?

00:03:07.070 --> 00:03:09.620
A bike race?

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:12.690
Yeah. It generates a lot 
of excitement every year.

00:03:12.690 --> 00:03:14.710
I'm on the executive committee, too.

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:19.810
This year's favorite is 
third-year Dan Fia Elgar,

00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:22.450
but a lot of people have 
their eye on first-year Jilk.

00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:25.720
He's nothing if not skilled 
at handling an air bike.

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:28.470
Mr. Leon isn't going to participate?

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:33.980
Leon's skilled enough to race, 
but he's much more likely...

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:35.880
...to bet on the race.

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:43.360
I hope he doesn't develop too 
much of an interest in gambling.

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:44.710
I couldn't agree more.

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:51.550
If Jilk wins this race, we'll win a 
significant amount of prize money.

00:03:51.550 --> 00:03:53.750
Why don't you try betting on the race?

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:56.380
I don't like gambling.

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:59.810
Go! That's it!

00:03:57.410 --> 00:04:02.420
<i>In my previous life, the man I dated 
constantly owed gambling debts.</i>

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:06.390
<i>So in this world, I'll earn my money 
through more reliable methods.</i>

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:09.750
Now let's get to work.

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:13.770
Fine, then. I'll work hard to earn my pay.

00:04:14.110 --> 00:04:16.270
You didn't need to say that.

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:18.960
Go, go!

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:20.160
Pass him!

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:22.360
That's it!

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:26.820
<i>Number 6 is in first, with number 7 in second!</i>

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:29.330
<i>Number 4 is catching up!</i>

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:36.510
Several riders appear to be trying 
to help certain others win.

00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:39.710
As I expected, it should be numbers 6 and 4.

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:45.230
Bless you, Luxion. My winnings keep doubling.

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:49.660
You seem awfully 
engrossed in your wagers.

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:52.010
Someday you'll suffer for it.

00:04:52.010 --> 00:04:54.980
It's all right. I won't lose.

00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:57.980
<i>Number 6 finishes first, number 4 second!</i>

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:01.730
I can't stop laughing!

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:04.740
At least try to maintain a human face.

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:09.020
<i>Currently in the lead is Jilk.</i>

00:05:09.020 --> 00:05:11.240
<i>No wonder he's one of the favorites to win!</i>

00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:16.000
<i>Jilk, you'd better make me a lot of money.</i>

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:24.510
<i>What's this? They seem to be 
targeting tournament favorite Jilk.</i>

00:05:24.910 --> 00:05:26.140
What?

00:05:26.140 --> 00:05:28.030
They're sticking right on him.

00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:29.750
Why would they do that?

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:33.480
<i>Of course she's worried about him.</i>

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:37.640
<i>In the game, they could end up together.</i>

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:43.330
The riders getting in his 
way are Clarice's followers.

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:45.530
Clarice? You mean...

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:54.040
<i>An impressive loop by Jilk!</i>

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:56.210
<i>He's so fast!</i>

00:05:58.010 --> 00:06:02.040
<i>Jilk finishes in first place! 
What a marvelous race!</i>

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:03.380
That was amazing!

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:05.050
I knew you could do it!

00:06:05.050 --> 00:06:07.930
Well, he didn't disappoint.

00:06:16.490 --> 00:06:18.690
Wh-What do you suppose happened?

00:06:19.160 --> 00:06:21.540
They hit him pretty hard.

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:23.660
He could be hurt.

00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:26.730
Jilk!

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:33.700
It's all right, Ms. Marie. 
It's just a broken bone.

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:39.120
But... But... My prize money!

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:41.320
He won't be able to participate 
in the next race.

00:06:41.320 --> 00:06:43.880
If Lord Jilk can't race, then...

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:46.340
There aren't any other first-year racers.

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:49.490
We'll have to find a substitute.

00:06:53.590 --> 00:06:57.980
My, my. You're looking 
rather miserable, Jilk.

00:06:58.210 --> 00:06:59.560
Clarice...

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:02.980
So you're responsible for 
the interference after all.

00:07:03.220 --> 00:07:07.990
Yes, that's right. And you'll suffer 
even worse for daring to leave me.

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:09.880
<i>Ms. Clarice...</i>

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:12.490
<i>She's Jilk's ex-fiancée.</i>

00:07:13.180 --> 00:07:16.890
<i>In the game, she looked a little 
more like an honor student.</i>

00:07:18.730 --> 00:07:21.460
Pretty girls are intense when they're angry.

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:25.130
Don't make fun of people! No!

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:26.510
No!

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:31.260
<i>What is she doing? That's so cute!</i>

00:07:31.480 --> 00:07:36.140
Clarice, I understand how you feel, 
but it wasn't necessary to go that far.

00:07:36.140 --> 00:07:40.130
Angelica, how can you look so unconcerned?

00:07:40.130 --> 00:07:42.460
Didn't the prince dump you?

00:07:42.830 --> 00:07:46.650
You're putting on quite the show 
with your personal slaves in tow.

00:07:47.310 --> 00:07:50.150
Do you fancy yourself the 
heroine of some tragedy?

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:53.540
Sh-Shut up! You don't know me!

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:56.270
Miss, you're speaking 
to the count's daughter.

00:07:58.820 --> 00:08:03.000
Jilk, I'm never going to 
stop getting revenge on you.

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:05.040
You'd better beg for forgiveness.

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:08.550
If that will settle your feelings.

00:08:09.020 --> 00:08:12.300
But if you do anything to Ms. Marie, 
you will pay the price.

00:08:16.020 --> 00:08:19.340
Miss, nothing good comes from revenge.

00:08:19.340 --> 00:08:21.430
There's surely something 
more important you could—

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:23.810
You don't know what you're talking about!

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:26.440
Yes, miss! I'm sorry, miss!

00:08:27.220 --> 00:08:31.260
<i>This girl's just like my little 
sister from my previous life.</i>

00:08:32.660 --> 00:08:37.910
Jilk, I'll never forgive you, no matter what.

00:08:40.780 --> 00:08:41.880
What will you do?

00:08:42.210 --> 00:08:45.460
It seems like we'll have to find 
a substitute for the next race.

00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:48.070
No, I'll participate in the race.

00:08:48.070 --> 00:08:50.460
It's the smartest choice.

00:08:50.950 --> 00:08:54.720
<i>The smartest choice would've been 
not calling off your engagement.</i>

00:08:54.730 --> 00:08:56.840
You should race in his place.

00:08:57.120 --> 00:08:58.970
What? Why me?

00:08:59.290 --> 00:09:00.620
Because the prize money—

00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:07.480
No, wait. I mean, because she'll be in 
trouble if there's no first-year racer.

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:08.730
She's right.

00:09:08.730 --> 00:09:11.970
If an executive committee member 
can't even find a substitute...

00:09:11.970 --> 00:09:14.990
People will question the 
duke's daughter's competence.

00:09:15.560 --> 00:09:18.270
Leon, don't worry about me.

00:09:18.270 --> 00:09:21.010
I can't cause any more trouble for you.

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:26.370
<i>Angie's paying for protecting me, isn't she?</i>

00:09:27.010 --> 00:09:29.880
<i>I owe Angie's dad a huge favor.</i>

00:09:30.440 --> 00:09:33.380
<i>If I cause any trouble for her...</i>

00:09:37.310 --> 00:09:38.890
I'll race.

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:40.000
What?

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:41.140
Leon...

00:09:41.670 --> 00:09:44.130
Rejoice, you green scoundrel.

00:09:44.130 --> 00:09:46.390
I'll win the tournament for you.

00:09:47.340 --> 00:09:50.460
It seems I have no choice 
but to rely on you now.

00:09:50.830 --> 00:09:53.030
This will undoubtedly be 
a large debt to pay.

00:09:53.030 --> 00:09:55.540
Oh, yeah. And you'll be 
paying me back right away.

00:09:55.540 --> 00:09:56.850
You'd better be ready.

00:09:59.190 --> 00:10:00.980
It's time for the finals.

00:10:00.980 --> 00:10:02.900
But Jilk isn't racing, right?

00:10:02.900 --> 00:10:05.040
Mr. Dan's going to win.

00:10:06.740 --> 00:10:08.670
You're really pushing yourself, aren't you?

00:10:09.030 --> 00:10:11.920
You've fully become one 
of Angelica's followers.

00:10:12.370 --> 00:10:15.400
I'm not worthy of being a 
duke's daughter's follower.

00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:17.630
I just know my place as a mob—

00:10:16.820 --> 00:10:18.600
So you're the substitute, huh?

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:26.560
Oh? What business does tournament 
favorite Mr. Dan have with me?

00:10:26.910 --> 00:10:29.800
I can't believe the shovel knight 
is racing in Jilk's place.

00:10:30.150 --> 00:10:32.030
Though I bear no grudge against you,

00:10:32.030 --> 00:10:34.320
I'll crush you with everything 
I've got in the next race.

00:10:34.620 --> 00:10:37.320
Did Lady Clarice threaten you?

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:38.780
No!

00:10:40.890 --> 00:10:47.080
She's actually a kind person. 
Her followers looked up to her.

00:10:47.970 --> 00:10:51.130
Her home has a racetrack.

00:10:51.130 --> 00:10:53.710
She looked after Jilk, too.

00:10:54.690 --> 00:10:57.430
She looked so beautiful 
as she cheered him on.

00:10:58.490 --> 00:11:01.450
It was a source of both 
frustration and joy for us.

00:11:02.550 --> 00:11:06.030
But Jilk suddenly called 
off their engagement.

00:11:06.030 --> 00:11:09.730
All he gave her was a single letter. 
He won't even meet with her.

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:12.660
He deserves a beating for that.

00:11:12.660 --> 00:11:19.340
I hate Jilk, too. In other words, 
you and I both hate hot guys.

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:21.860
So, whaddya say? Why don't 
you let me off the hook?

00:11:23.310 --> 00:11:26.120
I'm sorry, but Lady Clarice's 
orders are absolute.

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:28.420
Aw, man. No, huh?

00:11:29.180 --> 00:11:33.140
Lady Clarice is more popular than I thought.

00:11:33.560 --> 00:11:36.300
I've finished modifying the bike.

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:39.260
Are you still going to try to 
win after what he told you?

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:43.060
Of course I am. I bet a 
ton of money on myself.

00:11:43.060 --> 00:11:45.130
Plus, I'll get to see the frustration

00:11:45.130 --> 00:11:48.270
and disappointment of 
everyone who thinks I'll lose.

00:11:50.150 --> 00:11:52.520
I'd happily win to see that.

00:11:52.760 --> 00:11:58.270
You don't give off the slightest impression 
of using my strength to win.

00:11:58.270 --> 00:12:00.040
I strive to be as audacious.

00:12:00.040 --> 00:12:02.530
Don't you think you hate 
me a little too much?

00:12:07.630 --> 00:12:09.410
<i>It's time for the final race.</i>

00:12:09.900 --> 00:12:12.910
<i>The favorite to win is third-year Dan.</i>

00:12:13.740 --> 00:12:15.420
<i>Let the final race...</i>

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:19.550
<i>Begin!</i>

00:12:23.430 --> 00:12:25.370
We're surrounded.

00:12:25.370 --> 00:12:27.550
Just how much do these guys love me?

00:12:29.090 --> 00:12:31.490
<i>Oh? Looks like they're going after Leon!</i>

00:12:30.320 --> 00:12:32.510
Whoa! What are these guys doing?

00:12:32.510 --> 00:12:34.560
They're not even Lady Clarice's followers.

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:36.380
I'm in debt because of you!

00:12:36.380 --> 00:12:37.560
Die!

00:12:36.710 --> 00:12:37.560
You fiend!

00:12:37.880 --> 00:12:38.830
Damn it.

00:12:38.830 --> 00:12:40.490
Karma's a bitch.

00:12:40.490 --> 00:12:41.320
Shut up.

00:12:41.650 --> 00:12:42.670
Take this!

00:12:42.040 --> 00:12:43.820
<i>Leon's in trouble!</i>

00:12:42.670 --> 00:12:43.820
Come on, fall!

00:12:44.120 --> 00:12:45.140
Get him!

00:12:45.140 --> 00:12:46.100
Crush him!

00:12:46.100 --> 00:12:47.820
<i>Yeah, get him!</i>

00:12:47.820 --> 00:12:49.950
Commentator, you asshole!

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:52.950
It's your own fault you're 
in debt. <i>You</i> guys can fall!

00:12:54.630 --> 00:12:55.960
Hup!

00:13:00.680 --> 00:13:01.790
Did you see that?

00:13:01.790 --> 00:13:05.720
I'm experiencing something firsthand that only 
occurs when everyone's on the same level.

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:07.230
Someone stop Bartfort!

00:13:07.230 --> 00:13:07.920
That's it!

00:13:07.920 --> 00:13:09.160
Hit him again!

00:13:09.160 --> 00:13:10.810
Stop him!

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:12.410
This is even worse than I expected.

00:13:12.410 --> 00:13:14.510
I feel sorry for Mr. Leon.

00:13:14.510 --> 00:13:16.230
Serves him right.

00:13:17.150 --> 00:13:20.480
People really hate your follower.

00:13:22.810 --> 00:13:25.240
Leon isn't my follower.

00:13:25.240 --> 00:13:27.730
That's not important.

00:13:27.730 --> 00:13:31.740
Do you have any idea how much my family 
has suffered because of you people?

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:36.290
Shouldn't you be directing your resentment 
toward your own thoughtlessness?

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:37.620
Bitch!

00:13:41.640 --> 00:13:43.880
Please stop being mean to Angie!

00:13:43.880 --> 00:13:47.130
Stay out of this, commoner!

00:13:48.150 --> 00:13:49.390
Livia...

00:13:49.390 --> 00:13:51.720
What's gotten into you, Angelica?

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:54.910
You used to look down on commoners.

00:13:54.910 --> 00:13:56.390
I guess people do change.

00:13:56.390 --> 00:13:58.390
I-I...

00:13:58.390 --> 00:14:03.150
You acted like commoners weren't people.

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:09.910
Or do you enjoy watching her being 
tormented right in front of you?

00:14:09.910 --> 00:14:11.010
What?

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:12.980
Angie...

00:14:13.690 --> 00:14:15.290
N-No...

00:14:15.910 --> 00:14:17.290
Livia!

00:14:19.940 --> 00:14:22.670
<i>Do I have any right to chase after her?</i>

00:14:23.310 --> 00:14:26.420
<i>It's true that I previously felt that way.</i>

00:14:26.420 --> 00:14:29.590
Aw, she ran away.

00:14:29.590 --> 00:14:32.430
I guess your last friend 
was a cold bitch, too.

00:14:34.550 --> 00:14:37.180
What the hell do you know?!

00:14:40.190 --> 00:14:40.740
Hey...

00:14:40.740 --> 00:14:41.870
What's going on?

00:14:41.030 --> 00:14:42.940
N-Now you've done it!

00:14:42.940 --> 00:14:44.940
Trifling bitch!

00:14:45.330 --> 00:14:47.440
Stay away from me!

00:14:49.620 --> 00:14:50.950
Damn you!

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:54.700
You shrew! Don't get ahead of yourself 
when your family's on the decline!

00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:58.080
Please stop!

00:14:58.080 --> 00:15:00.030
Both of you have crossed the line!

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:05.210
<i>Something's wrong with Bartfort!</i>

00:15:06.050 --> 00:15:07.720
Now you can't race anymore!

00:15:07.720 --> 00:15:09.470
All bark, no bite. Later, loser!

00:15:09.690 --> 00:15:11.450
You ready to go, Luxion?

00:15:11.450 --> 00:15:15.540
I'm ready anytime. However, don't 
you think people hate you too much?

00:15:15.540 --> 00:15:17.220
They can hate me all they want.

00:15:17.600 --> 00:15:20.730
They can break my body, 
but they can't break my heart!

00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:24.730
<i>What's this?</i>

00:15:24.980 --> 00:15:28.250
<i>Bartfort has suddenly accelerated!</i>

00:15:28.250 --> 00:15:31.740
<i>I don't believe it! How is he going so fast?</i>

00:15:32.270 --> 00:15:33.490
Can we catch them?

00:15:33.490 --> 00:15:35.620
Don't you mean "pass them"?

00:15:39.430 --> 00:15:40.900
<i>What a shocking turn of events!</i>

00:15:40.900 --> 00:15:44.270
<i>Bartfort has joined the race for first!</i>

00:15:44.270 --> 00:15:45.220
No!

00:15:45.220 --> 00:15:46.500
Bastard!

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:49.330
You guys hate the idea 
of me winning that much?

00:15:49.330 --> 00:15:51.380
Well, now I <i>have</i> to win!

00:15:51.380 --> 00:15:53.070
You're not going anywhere!

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:55.890
Too bad.

00:15:55.890 --> 00:15:56.890
Whoa!

00:15:56.650 --> 00:15:57.420
Idiot!

00:15:56.890 --> 00:15:58.390
Stay away!

00:15:59.710 --> 00:16:01.640
Bye-bye.

00:16:01.970 --> 00:16:03.020
This is the end.

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:05.270
<i>Bartfort is currently in second place!</i>

00:16:05.730 --> 00:16:07.770
That just leaves Mr. Dan.

00:16:09.030 --> 00:16:10.960
<i>Bartfort has caught up to him!</i>

00:16:10.960 --> 00:16:13.280
<i>Who's going to win?!</i>

00:16:13.550 --> 00:16:15.600
Bring it on! It'll be a contest of skill!

00:16:15.600 --> 00:16:17.020
Mr. Dan...

00:16:17.430 --> 00:16:19.510
Sorry, but I'm gonna pass on that!

00:16:24.140 --> 00:16:26.370
It's so fast! I'm scared!

00:16:26.370 --> 00:16:30.420
I'm never racing again!

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:32.690
<i>Goal!</i>

00:16:34.150 --> 00:16:39.180
<i>Th-The winner is... Bartfort!</i>

00:16:40.010 --> 00:16:41.550
You again?

00:16:41.550 --> 00:16:43.630
What a pest!

00:16:43.630 --> 00:16:45.600
Die!

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:48.140
Sorry, guys.

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:49.490
Master.

00:16:49.490 --> 00:16:52.690
What is it? I feel great 
right now. Leave me alone.

00:16:53.050 --> 00:16:56.710
Understood, but the bike 
has reached its limit.

00:16:56.710 --> 00:16:57.730
Huh?

00:16:57.730 --> 00:16:59.390
You did ride rather recklessly.

00:17:03.140 --> 00:17:05.710
No! I'm gonna die!

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:08.210
Mr. Dan...

00:17:09.770 --> 00:17:13.470
Mr. Dan, you saved me.

00:17:14.450 --> 00:17:15.840
Don't worry about it.

00:17:16.380 --> 00:17:20.100
After all, we both hate hot guys.

00:17:20.410 --> 00:17:21.750
Mr. Dan...

00:17:30.190 --> 00:17:31.610
Platinum coins...

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:37.610
It's time for you to repay 
your debt, my dear Jilk.

00:17:38.020 --> 00:17:41.530
Very well. Order me to do whatever you wish.

00:17:41.530 --> 00:17:43.610
I shall follow it to the 
best of my abilities.

00:17:43.960 --> 00:17:47.090
What are you going to make 
him do? A naked handstand?

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:52.680
That's not a bad idea.

00:17:52.680 --> 00:17:55.220
I bet making him do that in front of 
the girls would earn me some money.

00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:58.110
Are you that desperate for money, you miser?!

00:17:58.110 --> 00:17:59.010
Take a look in a mirror!

00:17:59.010 --> 00:18:00.670
You're even more of a miser than I am!

00:17:59.580 --> 00:18:02.260
So, what should I do?

00:18:00.670 --> 00:18:03.340
More importantly, give 
me back my prize money!

00:18:02.260 --> 00:18:05.190
Ah, right. I want you to...

00:18:07.770 --> 00:18:12.020
I'm terribly sorry for what I did.

00:18:13.190 --> 00:18:18.780
I am sorry, Clarice. I truly believe 
what I did to you was terrible.

00:18:19.640 --> 00:18:23.280
It's too late! I waited so long for you, too!

00:18:23.540 --> 00:18:27.010
Did you think a single letter could 
make it like nothing had ever happened?

00:18:27.010 --> 00:18:30.060
I didn't want to lie to you.

00:18:30.680 --> 00:18:33.910
I've fallen in love with another woman.

00:18:37.620 --> 00:18:43.300
You what? Why? Why can't it be me?

00:18:44.850 --> 00:18:50.310
I don't know either, but I've 
fallen in love with Marie.

00:18:50.610 --> 00:18:53.520
<i>It sounds nice coming from 
him because he's so handsome,</i>

00:18:53.520 --> 00:18:56.570
<i>but basically, he didn't want to see 
her because it was a pain in the ass.</i>

00:18:56.570 --> 00:18:58.640
How dare you—

00:18:58.640 --> 00:18:59.920
Forget it.

00:18:59.920 --> 00:19:01.060
My lady?

00:19:01.060 --> 00:19:03.330
He's not worth dirtying your hands.

00:19:04.840 --> 00:19:08.580
I'm through associating with that man.

00:19:16.290 --> 00:19:20.340
Thank you, my lord.

00:19:20.610 --> 00:19:24.850
It's fine. I did it because 
I don't like Jilk, either.

00:19:26.520 --> 00:19:29.970
And Lady Clarice, get back 
on your feet already.

00:19:30.500 --> 00:19:33.230
There are plenty more fish in the sea.

00:19:33.980 --> 00:19:39.110
Thank you. You've got a twisted 
personality, but you're a kind person.

00:19:41.590 --> 00:19:45.370
Leon, you should go to your friends.

00:19:45.630 --> 00:19:46.370
Huh?

00:19:46.370 --> 00:19:51.020
A lot happened to both Angie and the 
scholarship student during the race.

00:19:57.970 --> 00:19:59.480
You seem down.

00:20:00.610 --> 00:20:01.810
Mr. Leon...

00:20:04.010 --> 00:20:06.260
Angie explained the situation to me.

00:20:07.150 --> 00:20:12.270
Mr. Leon, do you think 
Angie and I can be friends?

00:20:16.360 --> 00:20:20.650
Do you mind if I'm honest 
with you? It'll be pretty harsh.

00:20:23.460 --> 00:20:25.160
Please.

00:20:25.160 --> 00:20:29.790
The short answer is it'll 
be incredibly difficult.

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:33.720
Your living environments are just too 
different. You have nothing in common.

00:20:34.440 --> 00:20:38.230
Frankly, I think things had 
been going too smoothly so far.

00:20:40.710 --> 00:20:46.090
I was so happy to have finally 
made a friend at the academy.

00:20:48.580 --> 00:20:52.270
But it seems it won't work out.

00:20:56.370 --> 00:20:59.790
Angie's lost followers since the duel.

00:20:59.790 --> 00:21:03.530
It was probably convenient for her that 
you and I were friendly toward her.

00:21:03.530 --> 00:21:06.280
A-Angie isn't that kind of person!

00:21:08.220 --> 00:21:12.290
Then you'll be fine. You know that, don't you?

00:21:14.620 --> 00:21:17.290
Mr. Leon, you really are a mean person.

00:21:17.780 --> 00:21:20.330
I'm not like the prince or Jilk.

00:21:20.330 --> 00:21:23.420
It'd seem like a joke if I tried 
to suavely cheer you up.

00:21:24.680 --> 00:21:28.180
I'm going to try talking to Angie again.

00:21:28.530 --> 00:21:30.820
Good choice.

00:21:38.340 --> 00:21:42.740
<i>As long as I communicate my feelings, 
I'm sure even Angie and I can be friends.</i>

00:21:44.660 --> 00:21:45.650
Yes?

00:21:50.840 --> 00:21:52.160
Do you have a minute?

00:21:55.120 --> 00:21:57.790
<b>Trapped in a Dating Sim</b>

00:23:25.740 --> 00:23:27.140
Pirate hunting, huh?

00:23:27.140 --> 00:23:30.260
Hunting down pirates is 
a noble's job. I'm in.

00:23:30.260 --> 00:23:32.290
It's our turn at bat.

00:23:32.290 --> 00:23:35.160
Next time: "This Isn't a Game."

00:23:35.160 --> 00:23:36.760
So I'm leading these two idiots, huh?

00:23:37.020 --> 00:23:38.060
What does that mean?

00:23:38.060 --> 00:23:40.020
Yeah, I still hate this guy.
